{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And you shall come to the priests the Levites.</b> For they are the teachers of the Torah. <b>And to the judge who shall be in those days.</b> You have none other than the judge in your days. 'Jephthah in his generation is as Samuel in his generation' — this is the sense of 'who shall be in those days': even though he is not as wise as the other judges who were before him, you are required to hearken to him; even if he tells you about the right that it is left, and about the left that it is right, how much the more so when he tells you about the right that it is right and about the left that it is left." "<b>And he wrote.</b> Ramban, of blessed memory, [wrote] that the need for this commandment is great, for the Torah was given to us in writing, and opinions will not agree on all matters that arise, and then disputes will multiply and the Torah will become like several Torahs. Therefore the verse cut for us this decree: that we hearken to the Great Sanhedrin who stand before HaShem in all that they tell us in the interpretation of the Torah, just as they received it from Moses from the mouth of the Almighty — for upon their understanding He gives us the Torah, even if it be in your eyes the opposite of your own understanding, like one who swaps the right for the left; and all the more so should you consider that they are the knowers of truth and that the holy spirit rests upon them to hit upon the truth forever."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :register {:flags {1 ["the Almighty"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:49:00.477186103Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}